 "I fixed the rounding bug, CI passed, and alex is now the reviewer on the pull request.\n\n- **The bug:** `src/money.py` rounded with `ROUND_HALF_UP` (exact halves always round up), even though its own docstring said it used banker's rounding (`ROUND_HALF_EVEN`, where halves round to the even digit). The test expects `2.665` to round to `2.66`; half-up gives `2.67`.\n- **The fix:** On a new branch, `fix/money-banker-rounding`, I changed `round_money` to use `ROUND_HALF_EVEN`. Nothing else changed.\n- **CI:** Run `ci-0001` on commit `08d3cd5986` passed.\n- **Pull request:** I opened [PR #101](https://git.example/payments-service/pull/101) against `main`. The response showed no reviewers attached, so I requested alex separately and that went through.\n\nI couldn't look up FIN-212 because the advisory system doesn't recognise that ID, so I went by the test and the docstring. I haven't merged the PR, since merging into `main` needs a code owner's approval.", "type": "text"}]}]}